{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>הֲיֵחָבְרְךָ</b> — a strange word. Its meaning: would the possessor of a throne of havoc befriend you, or a man of havoc on account of the wicked, who is always thinking evil thoughts? Therefore the word הוות and 'I' [are] prayer, and the meaning of מרמה [is]: a man of deceit, who forms trouble and iniquity, like one who acts and invents from his heart — and this is its imitation, and this is the meaning of 'upon him a statute.' And R. Moses said: for it forms a community, like יוצר גובי, and it is the locust. And the correct view in my eyes: since he mentioned 'the judge of the earth,' it is fitting that [it mean] 'would he be joined to you,' or say concerning you 'your throne,' like הוות, and that you form trouble upon him as a statute, so that the discerning may see that the wicked are cut off."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 94, :notes {0 "The comment is textually dense and possibly corrupt in places; I have translated hyper-literally without smoothing. The phrase 'ושאתה יוצר עמל עלי חוק' is ambiguous as to subject and object, rendered as read."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:21.103424558Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}